From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fanboy <fanboy@openwrt.org>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: warn instead of splatting on reg fallback

ath12k_reg_handle_chan_list() falls back to re-sending the previous
country setting when a regulatory channel list event cannot be
processed, and then hits a bare WARN_ON(1).  On QCN9274 boards the
firmware sends an empty ruleset during the boot-time regulatory update,
so every boot produces a full kernel splat even though the fallback
does its job and the radios come up.

Replace the WARN_ON(1) with a dev-level warning.  The fallback path and
the surrounding "No reg rules available" / "failed to extract
regulatory info" messages are unchanged.  This mirrors the in-function
TODO which already acknowledges the case needs proper handling
upstream.

Signed-off-by: fanboy <fanboy@openwrt.org>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
@@ -6994,7 +6994,7 @@
 	 * reverted at the fw and the old SCAN_CHAN_LIST cmd needs to be sent.
 	 */
 	/* TODO: This is rare, but still should also be handled */
-	WARN_ON(1);
+	ath12k_warn(ab, "failed to process regulatory channel list event\n");
 
 out:
 	/* In some error cases, even a valid pdev_idx might not be available */
